# star_wars_elg 1.10 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1271) from the Spike 2 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port.
# Functions matched across the two builds: 3142 of 22107 reference functions (1628 anchored by vtable slots and strings, the rest grown through calls).
# Written: the core and the globals the 64-bit runtime has run with (SITES_PROVEN, DATA_PROVEN); every other
# entry placed is a comment with its address, for when its runtime feature is made 64-bit.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-14 (PAD-1271) on the Spike 3 rig (s3run.sh, PAD_S3_MODE_SO = a 64-bit build of
# template_mode.c): the runtime hooked every site below, the Insider gate armed (achievement query type 28), and
# in play TARGET RUSH started on three Death star target hits (switch 26), scored 8 shots through the game's
# score_add (+36,000,000: the score table read 26,500 -> 36,083,880), ended on its clock, and got the end of
# ball from the bus (event 0x34). Program sha1 ceb8d70b73a63698d06afddfe571c1bbab775c0a (games/game).
# Sounds emulator-proven 2026-11-14 (PAD-1282, slot 82, muted, the PCM kept): a mode played request 153, callout 168
# and the countdown 170 -> 166 ("One!" .. "Five!", step -1) through the sites below, each taken by the game's worker,
# and sound_active / sound_stop / a fade on the 64-bit channel values answered as the PCM did.
# Lamps and light shows emulator-proven 2026-11-14 (PAD-1283, slot 1, hidden, muted, the bridge's dump/padled): a mode's
# light_insert blinked DEATH STAR (X2) / LEFT OUTLANE / RAMP 6 on the playfield board from its start to its end,
# light_all held all 67 inserts at 255, light_shots blinked the 3 tied to its scoring shots; the game's shows 1-5
# played as process 13201 (stopped at their length through event_cancel), and the game's layer list lost each show's
# group as it ended (the exit hook at +0x138 calling lamp_free_owner).
# Screens, words and clips emulator-proven 2026-11-14 (PAD-1284, slot 84, hidden, muted): a mode's own screen and its
# words were found in the HUD (find_node / find_text through x8, the scene at +0x38) and shown over the game's HUD for
# the mode (the Sprite's slot 42), and its title clip played full screen on the video bank's surface at its start
# (surface_find, surface_set_video, surface_play), on Try it and on a card write_card wrote.
# Multiball, held coils and blocks emulator-proven 2026-11-14 (PAD-1285, slot 85, hidden, muted): a mode file's
# `multiball 3 10` was served through multiball_serve (balls_in_play 3) and ran its full 40 s as the balls drained -
# no longer taken for one of the game's multiballs; its `coil_hold right_gate 2000` found node 8 coil 2 = the game's
# device 9, took the gate object (0x711730, control +40) through coil_take, sent ONE command (255 for 64 ms, then
# 128 for 1936 ms) through coil_fire and gave it back after 2007 ms through coil_give.
# PAD-1322 (2026-11-15, slot 91): the switch drain's edges are the shots (site switch_edge inside its loop, the record in
# x19): EDGE TEST started on three TOP LANE CENTER edges and scored six shots; the flipper buttons, slingshots and pop
# bumpers (no handler bits) are edges too.

game           star_wars_elg
version        1.10

